  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Multi-Purpose cash assistance (MPCA) to address the most critical needs of crisis-affected communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $3.9 million IOM project is to address the urgent needs of internally displaced people, their host communities and returnees affected by floods and sub-national violence. To that end, IOM will distribute more than $2.7 million in multi-purpose cash to 59,034 people. 10,200 people from this target caseload will additionally receive a one-time payment to cover urgent shelter and essential item needs. In total, IOM will reach 59,034 people with life-saving assistance, including 14,209 women, 16,331 girls, and 6,512 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
